[12.315, "o", "\u001b[2m📖 reading real --help of tar...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.215, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.365, "o", "\u001b[0;32mtar\u001b[0m is a utility for archiving files into a single file (called an archive) and extracting them later. It is commonly used for backup, distribution, and compression.\r\n\r\nCommon options:\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-c\u001b[0m Create a new archive.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-x\u001b[0m Extract files from an archive.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-t\u001b[0m List the contents of an archive.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-f\u001b[0m Specify the archive file name.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-v\u001b[0m Be verbose (show progress).\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-z\u001b[0m Compress the archive with gzip.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-j\u001b[0m Compress the archive with bzip2.\r\n- \u001b[0;32m-C\u001b[0m Change to a specific directory before processing files.\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\u001b[0;32m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\u001b[0m\r\ntar \u001b[1;36m-cvf\u001b[0m archive.tar /path/to/directory\r\ntar \u001b[1;36m-xvf\u001b[0m archive.tar\r\n\u001b[0;32m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\u001b[0m"]
